@host = https://localhost:7193

### 1. Categories — expect 9, ids 1–9, Food→Other
GET {{host}}/api/categories

### 2. Expenses list — expect []
GET {{host}}/api/expenses

### 3. Create expense — expect 201 + Location, categoryName "Food", amount 42.50
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "amount": 42.50,
  "description": "Lunch",
  "expenseDate": "2026-09-01"
}

### capture the created id for the requests below
@id = {{create.response.body.id}}

### 4. Get by id — expect 200, same expense
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/{{id}}

### 5. Get unknown id — expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 6. List again — expect one item
GET {{host}}/api/expenses

### 7. Update — expect 204; then GET shows Transport / 99.99 / updatedAt > createdAt
PUT {{host}}/api/expenses/{{id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 2,
  "amount": 99.99,
  "description": "Taxi",
  "expenseDate": "2026-09-02"
}

### 7b. Confirm the update
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/{{id}}

### 8. Update unknown id — expect 404
PUT {{host}}/api/expenses/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "amount": 1.00,
  "description": "x",
  "expenseDate": "2026-09-01"
}

### 9. Delete — expect 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/expenses/{{id}}

### 9b. Get after delete — expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/{{id}}

### 9c. List after delete — expect []
GET {{host}}/api/expenses

### 10. Delete unknown id — expect 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/expenses/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000